per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-mobius-nogo"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-mobius-nogo"],"id":"long.prop-mobius-nogo","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 10.10 (Möbius-support countermodel: the natural negative-sign candidate overshoots)","locator":"Long record Proposition 10.10, p. 118, label prop:mobius-nogo","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The signed Lambert identity $\\sum_{d\\ge1}\\mu(d)/(2^d-1) = 1/2$ is exact. Writing $N:=\\{d:\\mu(d)=-1\\}$: $\\sum_{d\\in N}1/(2^d-1) = 1/2 + \\sum_{d\\in P}1/(2^d-1)$ where $P:=\\{d\\ge2:\n\\mu(d)=1\\}$, and quantitatively $1/2 + 1/63 \\le \\sum_{d\\in N}1/(2^d-1)$ (using the first positive tail term $d=6$, $\\mu(6)=1$) ; the negative-Möbius support strictly *overshoots* $1/2$ by at least $1/63$.*\n\n***Scope.** Rules out exactly one natural candidate infinite Boolean support (the negative-Möbius set) as a witness for $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$. A route-sufficiency no-go only ; it says nothing about whether *some other* infinite Boolean support sums to $1/2$. **Object or representation:** about the *object* ; a genuine value inequality for one specific candidate set, not a coordinate artifact. Margin $1/63$ is the concrete number any repair attempt (adding/removing finitely many elements) must close or exceed.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"field:28f40e2f4b2cc7f9f9d4158d2cb269ab9a9cf7c5e601760f03617ca490932e11","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/sources/paper.long.pdf"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"field:344e23ce7579f7e81a14e448dbd787f21ac719517fe589cc6ec7feee059980d9","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3